WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.501
-Today is Friday. That's usually
when I catch up

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.701
on some personal stuff.
I check my inbox,

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.200
I return some e-mails,
and of course,

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.634
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.100
And I was just running a bit --

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah!

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:11.901
-I was running a bit behind
today so I thought,

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.167
if you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd like to write out

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:14.467
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:15.467
Is that cool with you?

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:18.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah!

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:21.467
Come on, man, yeah!

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.334
-J-James, can I get some
thank-you note writing --

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:25.200
You have to say it.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.300
-Yeah!
-Alright, there you go, yeah.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.934
[ Applause ]

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:37.901
♪♪

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:39.067
-Yeah!

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.200
♪♪

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.033
-Thank you,
"Thor: Love and Thunder" poster

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:49.133
for looking like how I feel when
I find my other AirPod.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.601
Thank you.

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:55.667
Thank you to the poster.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:56.968
-Hmm.
-Yeah!

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:58.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.868 --> 00:00:59.868
-It's going off the rails.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:01.167
♪♪

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:04.834
-Thank you, CNN+, shutting down
after 3 weeks.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.701
I guess if I want somewhere to
get my news 24 hours a day,

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:10.067
I'll just have to watch CNN.

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:13.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.267
♪♪

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:21.501
-Thank you, airplanes,
for immediately replacing

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:24.334
the dangers of COVID with
the dangers of Mike Tyson.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:27.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:30.868
-Ouch.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:32.467
♪♪

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:35.934
-Thank you, Coachella, for
looking like a Forever21

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.334
just took an edible.

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:40.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:45.968
♪♪

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:48.033
Thank you,
Netflix possibly launching

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:50.501
an ad-supported streaming plan,

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:52.400
though it's a little harder
to Netflix and chill

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:53.934
to the Stanley Steamer jingle.

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:56.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:02.067
What is that again?
-♪ 1-800-STEAMER ♪

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:04.934
-Both: ♪ Stanley Steamer
makes carpets cleaner ♪

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:06.434
-Yep.

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:07.501
I like --
-You like Rug Doctor.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:11.534
-♪ 1-800 and 588-2300 ♪

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:13.534
-Both: ♪ Empire ♪

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:15.501
-That's a -- That's fantastic.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.067
-I like, uh --
-I don't even know what they do,

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:18.200
but I want it.
-Yeah, you just want it.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:22.467
-Any jingles? Favorite jingles?

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:23.934
-It's too local, though.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.200
-Which one?

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.367
-Do you remember --
We had a show called "Ideal"

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.200
in the Tri-State Area.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.734
-"Ideal?"

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:34.300
-♪ If you got a passion
for fashion ♪

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.868
♪ If you got a cravings
for savings ♪

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:39.400
♪ Take the wheel
of your automobile ♪

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.234
♪ And swing on down to
"Ideal" ♪

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:45.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:48.000
-That's pretty good.
I don't know that one.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.400
I like it. I like that one.
That's good.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.567
[ Laughs ] ♪ Ideal ♪

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.467
♪♪

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:57.767
-Thank you, 4/20, for being
the second time this week

00:02:57.767 --> 00:03:01.000
people were convinced they saw
a giant bunny in a vest.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.367
-He's got a vest on, man.

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:08.567
♪♪

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:11.067
-Thank you, wedding rehearsals,
for saying,

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:12.968
"Take a good look because here's
what your wedding

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:15.300
would look like if everyone
wasn't wasted."

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.467
♪♪

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:25.400
Thank you, pomegranates,
for being a great snack

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.067
for people with 6 hours to kill.

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:30.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:35.868
♪♪

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:39.133
Thank you, surprise parties,
for officially confirming

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:41.467
that all of your friends have
a group chat without you.

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:44.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:49.234
-You lied to me.

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:50.934
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:52.234
♪♪

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.701
-Thank you, people that say
there's plenty of fish

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.400
in the sea after a breakup,
for basically saying,

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.601
"So, maybe humans
aren't for you?"

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:01.467
There you have it, everybody.
Those were my thank-you notes.

